{
  "milestones": [
    {
      "id": "m1",
      "title": "Implement dynamic exception in @reraise",
      "requests": [
        "R2"
      ],
      "requirement": "@reraise should accept a callable for the 'into' argument that returns the exception instance to raise, allowing dynamic exception construction.",
      "observable": "reraise(ValueError, lambda: ValueError('dynamic msg'))() raises ValueError with message 'dynamic msg'. reraise(ValueError, TypeError)() raises TypeError.",
      "public_names": [
        "reraise"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "why_requires": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "m2",
      "title": "Add has_path function",
      "requests": [
        "R4"
      ],
      "requirement": "Add a has_path(obj, path) function that checks if an object has a specific attribute path (e.g., 'a.b.c') without raising AttributeError.",
      "observable": "has_path({'a': {'b': 1}}, 'a.b') is True. has_path({'a': 1}, 'a.b') is False. has_path(1, 'x') is False.",
      "public_names": [
        "has_path"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "why_requires": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "m3",
      "title": "Unify memoize and cache invalidation API",
      "requests": [
        "R1"
      ],
      "requirement": "Ensure both @memoize and @cache decorated functions expose consistent invalidation methods: .invalidate(*args, **kwargs) and .invalidate_all(). Also ensure @memoize supports skipping via a mechanism compatible with existing usage (though R1 mentions .skip/.memory/.invalidate, the core unification is the API surface). Specifically, add invalidate and invalidate_all to memoize wrappers to match cache.",
      "observable": "dec = memoize(); dec.invalidate(); dec.invalidate_all(); dec.memory is accessible. dec_cache = cache(60); dec_cache.invalidate(); dec_cache.invalidate_all(); dec_cache.memory is NOT accessible (or behaves differently as per original, but R1 says unify, implying adding missing attrs to memoize). Let's stick to adding invalidate/invalidate_all to memoize.",
      "public_names": [
        "memoize",
        "cache"
      ],
      "requires": [],
      "why_requires": ""
    }
  ],
  "expected_causes": [
    "For m1: Developer might not realize 'into' can be a callable and only handle exception classes/instances.",
    "For m2: Developer might implement has_path incorrectly by using getattr with default instead of checking existence step-by-step, or fail to handle intermediate non-dict/non-object attributes correctly.",
    "For m3: Developer might forget to add invalidate/invalidate_all to memoize, or incorrectly copy the implementation from cache which uses datetime/timedelta logic, whereas memoize uses a simple dict."
  ],
  "verifier_plan": "Test m1 by calling reraise with a lambda and verifying the raised exception type and message. Test m2 by creating nested dicts/objects and checking various paths. Test m3 by decorating a function with @memoize and @cache, calling them, then calling .invalidate() and .invalidate_all() and verifying the cache/memory state is cleared appropriately."
}
